---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const rel = "https://github.com/jitendravjh/ghdeck/releases/latest/download";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="ghdeck, all your GitHub work in one list"
  description="A terminal dashboard for GitHub. PRs and issues together, newest first, with conflicts, CI and review state on every row."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>ghdeck</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      All your GitHub work in one list. PRs and issues together, newest first,
      with the status of each one sitting right there.
    </p>
    <p class="sub">
      GitHub splits these across two pages and neither tells you if a PR is
      conflicting or if CI has gone red. Other terminal dashboards keep PRs and
      issues in separate tabs. This one does not.
    </p>

    <div class="install">
      <code><span class="prompt">$ </span>brew install jitendravjh/tap/ghdeck</code>
    </div>
    <p class="hint">
      macOS and Linux. No Homebrew? <a href="/docs/#install">Grab a binary</a>, no Rust needed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="term">
    <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
    <pre><code><span class="tabs">ghdeck  <b>ATTENTION NEEDED [6]</b>  OPEN [12]  YOURS [111]  TO REVIEW [0]  ALL [130]</span>
<span class="sel"> <span class="d">1d</span>  <span class="b">[PR]</span>    <span class="d">kubernetes-sigs/headlamp#7128</span>  <span class="t">i18n: Complete Hindi translations</span>
             <span class="g">● open</span> <span class="d">·</span> <span class="r">✖ changes requested</span> <span class="d">·</span> <span class="y">◐ ci</span> <span class="d">·</span> <span class="y">@vyncent-t</span>   <span class="d">4 comments</span></span>
<span class="d">╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌</span>
 <span class="d">1d</span>  <span class="b">[PR]</span>    <span class="d">screenpipe/screenpipe#6449</span>  <span class="t">fix(meetings): lock transcription</span>
             <span class="g">● open</span> <span class="d">·</span> <span class="r">✖ ci</span>   <span class="d">6 comments</span>
<span class="d">╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌</span>
<span class="d">21h</span>  <span class="c">[ISSUE]</span> <span class="d">SciML/SciMLBenchmarks.jl#126</span>  <span class="t">Fix AdaptiveSDE benchmarks</span>
             <span class="r">✖ closed</span>   <span class="d">5 comments</span>
<span class="d">╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌</span>
<span class="d">21h</span>  <span class="b">[PR]</span>    <span class="d">SciML/SciMLBenchmarks.jl#1605</span>  <span class="t">Fix and update AdaptiveSDE (#126)</span>
             <span class="m">✔ merged</span>   <span class="d">37 comments</span>
<span class="d">╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌</span>
<span class="d">3mo</span>  <span class="b">[PR]</span>    <span class="d">SciML/NeuralOperators.jl#134</span>  <span class="t">feat: implement CNO (closes #122)</span>
             <span class="g">● open</span> <span class="d">·</span> <span class="r">! conflict</span>   <span class="d">2 comments</span></code></pre>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>An issue closing and the PR that closed it, side by side</h2>
    <p>
      That is the thing no other tool does. Everything you touched, sorted by
      when it last moved, with conflicts, failing CI and who you are waiting on
      all visible without opening anything.
    </p>
    <div class="grid" style="margin-top: 26px">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>One list</h3>
        <p>PRs and issues interleaved, newest first. Filter to what needs you, what is open, what is yours, what waits on your review.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Real status</h3>
        <p>Merge conflicts, CI rollup, review decisions and requested reviewers. GitHub search cannot even query conflicts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Read the thread</h3>
        <p>Press enter for the body, comments and reviews, with line comments under the review that made them. Bots collapse to one line.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Watches itself</h3>
        <p>Polls notifications with a conditional request. GitHub does not count 304s, so a quiet minute costs nothing at all.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="dash" />

  <section>
    <h2>Install</h2>
    <pre class="block"><span class="d"># macOS and Linux, with Homebrew</span>
brew install jitendravjh/tap/ghdeck

<span class="d"># or grab a binary, no Rust needed</span>
curl -sSfL {rel}/ghdeck-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz | tar xz
sudo mv ghdeck /usr/local/bin/</pre>
    <p style="margin-top:18px">
      Then <code>gh auth login</code>, or set a <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> with the
      <code>repo</code> scope, and run <code>ghdeck</code>. Full instructions in the
      <a href="/docs/">docs</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr class="dash" />

  <section>
    <h2>Keys</h2>
    <table class="keys">
      <tr><td>up down</td><td>move</td></tr>
      <tr><td>left right</td><td>switch filter</td></tr>
      <tr><td>enter</td><td>read the conversation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>o</td><td>open in browser</td></tr>
      <tr><td>/</td><td>search title, repo, label</td></tr>
      <tr><td>r</td><td>sync now</td></tr>
      <tr><td>?</td><td>help</td></tr>
    </table>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
